[0050] FIG. 1 illustrates a dual scalar/vector datapath processor according to a preferred embodiment of this invention. Processor 100 includes separate level one instruc- tion cache (L1I) 121 and level one data cache (L1D) 123. Processor 100 includes a level two combined instruction/ data cache (L2) 130 that holds both instructions and data. FIG. 1 illustrates connection between level one instruc- tion cache 121 and level two combined instruction/data cache 130 (bus 142). FIG. 1 illustrates connection between level one data cache 123 and level two combined instruction/data cache 130 (bus 145). In the preferred embodiment of pro- cessor 100 level two combined instruction/data cache 130 stores both instructions to back up level one instruction cache 121 and data to back up level one data cache 123. In the preferred embodiment level two combined instruction/ data cache 130 is further connected to higher level cache and/or main memory in a manner not illustrated in FIG. 1. In the preferred embodiment central processing unit core 110, level one instruction cache 121, level one data cache 123 and level two combined instruction/data cache 130 are formed on a single integrated circuit. This signal integrated circuit optionally includes other circuits.
[0051] Central processing unit core 110 fetches instruc- tions from level one instruction cache 121 as controlled by instruction fetch unit 111. Instruction fetch unit 111 deter- mines the next instructions to be executed and recalls a fetch packet sized set of such instructions. The nature and size of fetch packets are further detailed below. As known in the art, instructions are directly fetched from level one instruction cache 121 upon a cache hit (if these instructions are stored in level one instruction cache 121). Upon a cache miss (the specified instruction fetch packet is not stored in level one instruction cache 121), these instructions are sought in level two combined cache 130. In the preferred embodiment the size of a cache line in level one instruction cache 121 equals the size of a fetch packet. The memory locations of these instructions are either a hit in level two combined cache 130 or a miss. A hit is serviced from level two combined cache 130. A miss is serviced from a higher level of cache (not illustrated) or from main memory (not illustrated). As is known in the art, the requested instruction may be simulta- neously supplied to both level one instruction cache 121 and central processing unit core 110 to speed use.
[0052] In the preferred embodiment of this invention, central processing unit core 110 includes plural functional units to perform instruction specified data processing tasks. Instruction dispatch unit 112 determines the target functional unit of each fetched instruction. In the preferred embodiment central processing unit 110 operates as a very long instruc- tion word (VLIW) processor capable of operating on plural instructions in corresponding functional units simultane- ously. Preferably a complier organizes instructions in execute packets that are executed together. Instruction dis- patch unit 112 directs each instruction to its target functional unit. The functional unit assigned to an instruction is com- pletely specified by the instruction produced by a compiler. The hardware of central processing unit core 110 has no part in this functional unit assignment. In the preferred embodi- ment instruction dispatch unit 112 may operate on plural instructions in parallel. The number of such parallel instruc- tions is set by the size of the execute packet. This will be further detailed below.
[0053] One part of the dispatch task of instruction dispatch unit 112 is determining whether the instruction is to execute on a functional unit in scalar datapath side A 115 or vector datapath side B 116. An instruction bit within each instruc- tion called the s bit determines which datapath the instruc- tion controls. This will be further detailed below.
[0054] Instruction decode unit 113 decodes each instruc- tion in a current execute packet. Decoding includes identi- fication of the functional unit performing the instruction,

Claims: 1. A device comprising:
a processor functional unit having a predetermined vector size; and
a cache memory controller coupled to the processor functional unit and capable of:
receiving a set of parameters associated with a first set of data;
retrieving the first set of data;
in a first mode of operation, producing a second set of data by duplicating the first set of data by a first amount that is based on the predetermined vector size of the processor functional unit;
in a second mode of operation, producing the second set of data by duplicating the first set of data by a second amount that is based on the set of parameters irrespective of the predetermined vector size of the processor functional unit; and
providing the second set of data to the processor functional unit.
2. The device of claim 1, wherein, in the first mode of operation:
the set of parameters includes a vector length size; and
the first amount by which to duplicate the first set of data is based on a ratio of the predetermined vector size to the vector length size in the set of parameters.
3. The device of claim 1, wherein, in the second mode of operation, the set of parameters specifies the second amount by which to duplicate the first set of data.
4. The device of claim 1, wherein, in the first mode of operation, the producing of the second set of data includes padding the first set of data based on an unpadded second set of data being less than the predetermined vector size.
5. The device of claim 4, wherein the padding of the second set of data includes adding a padding value between a first instance of the first set of data and a second instance of the first set of data.
6. The device of claim 1, wherein the cache memory controller is capable of, in a third mode of operation, producing the second set of data by:
performing a first duplication of the first set of data by a third amount that is based on the predetermined vector size of the processor functional unit; and
performing a second duplication of the first set of data by a fourth amount that is based on the set of parameters irrespective of the predetermined vector size of the processor functional unit.
7. The device of claim 1 further comprising a level-two (L2) cache memory coupled to the cache memory controller, wherein the cache memory controller is capable of retrieving the first set of data from the L2 cache memory.
8. The device of claim 1, wherein the cache memory controller includes:
a first register capable of storing the first set of data;
a second register capable of storing the second set of data; and
a set of multiplexers coupled between the first register and the second register, wherein the set of multiplexers is capable of producing the second set of data using the first set of data in the first mode of operation and in the second mode of operation.
9. The device of claim 1 further comprising a register capable of storing the set of parameters, wherein the processor functional unit is capable of, in response to an instruction that specifies the register, cause the cache memory controller to retrieve the set of data.
10. The device of claim 1, wherein:
in the first mode of operation, in the second set of data, a first instance of a first element of the first set of data is separated from a second instance of the first element by an instance of a second element of the first set of data that is different from the first element; and
in the second mode of operation, in the second set of data, a first instance of a third element of the first set of data is adjacent to a second instance of the third element in the second set of data.
11. A device comprising:
a memory capable of storing a set of data;
a processor that includes a vector unit that has a prede- termined vector size; and
a memory controller coupled between the memory and the processor, wherein the processor is capable of causing the memory controller to:
retrieve a first set of data from the memory;
in a first mode of operation, perform a first duplication operation on the first set of data to produce a second set of data according to a first duplication factor that is based on the predetermined vector size;
in a second mode of operation, perform a second duplication operation on the first set of data to produce the second set of data according to a second duplication factor that is independent of the prede- termined vector size; and
provide the second set of data to the processor.
12. The device of claim 11, wherein the first duplication factor is based on a ratio of the predetermined vector size to a vector size of the first set of data.
13. The device of claim 11, wherein the processor is capable of causing the memory controller to receive the second duplication factor.
14. The device of claim 11, wherein, in the first mode of operation, the memory controller is capable of inserting a padding element in the second set of data based on an unpadded second set of data being less than the predetermined vector size.
15. The device of claim 14, wherein the padding element is between a first instance of a first element of the first set of data and a second instance of the first element.
16. The device of claim 11, wherein the processor is capable of causing the memory controller to, in a third mode of operation, perform the first duplication operation and the second duplication operation on the first set of data to produce the second set of data.
17. The device of claim 11, wherein the memory is a level-two (L2) cache memory.
18. A method comprising:
retrieving, from a memory, a first set of data;
determining whether to produce a second set of data by duplicating the first set of data by a first amount that is based on a predetermined vector size of a processor or by a second amount that is independent of the prede- termined vector size of the processor;
producing the second set of data; and
providing the second set of data to the processor.
19. The method of claim 18, wherein the first amount is based on a ratio of the predetermined vector size to a vector size of the first set of data.
20. The method of claim 18, wherein the producing of the second set of data includes padding the second set of data.

