Abstract: Training a flight instructor via actual flights with students by way of collecting data of a specific student and specific instructor then collecting the aircraft's flight metrics data during the same flight. Providing the server the data and providing weather data of the flight date including at least a Meteorological Aerodrome report (METAR) via a network in signal communication. The training server generates normalized values for each raw student performance metric to reflect one or more of the student experience, time of day, weather, and aircraft systems functional data; and, the training server is configured to use the normalized values and generate for the flight at least one of a numerical value for the specific one of a 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th and Nth student with 1st instructor performance a numerical value for the 1st instructor overall performance.

